Position allowlist (suggested)
Each returned position should contain only:
stake_id, project_code, status, principal_pi, recorded_reward_pi, started_at, unlock_at, is_matured;
capital_remaining_recorded_pi, reward_remaining_recorded_pi;
capital_requestable_pi, reward_requestable_pi;
capital_open_request_status, reward_open_request_status; and
any explicit eligibility issue code needed for a blocked position.
Each recent withdrawal should contain only request ID, stake ID, project code, type, requested amount, fee rate/amount, net amount, status, transaction ID, created/updated timestamps, and network. No private keys, access tokens, service-role secrets, or unneeded user data.
8. Wallet UI V1 behavior
Mainnet badge and verified-account status.
Balance cards with the definitions above; no generic “cash balance” or “Pi wallet balance” label.
Hide/show balance toggle, loading/error/empty states, and explicit last-updated time.
Position cards showing project, principal, reward, maturity, requestable amount, and status.
Recent activity preview with a link to the existing transactions.html.
Withdrawal call-to-action only links to the existing withdrawal workflow; it does not pay, approve, or directly transfer Pi.
If the registered withdrawal destination is missing or inconsistent with the current Pi Auth Core session address, show the issue and do not claim that withdrawal is ready.
No LocalStorage/sessionStorage financial records. UI-only preference state such as hide/show balance may be in memory; it must never affect financial computation.
9. Implementation gates and tests
Before implementing the endpoint and page:
Agree the reward settlement rule for capital_withdrawn positions.
Review a safe server-side way to compare the authenticated wallet address with the stored withdrawal destination.
Implement the endpoint as additive code only; no direct browser queries to private financial tables.
Unit-test the summary builder with synthetic fixtures without writing Mainnet rows.
Test all status combinations (pending, approved, paid, rejected, cancelled) and ensure fee deduction is never counted twice.
Test partial withdrawal, full withdrawal, a request in flight, maturity boundaries, missing address, address mismatch, empty account, malformed response, and API failure.
Verify Mainnet requests fail closed for Testnet and that no Mainnet data appears on Testnet.
Verify no endpoint starts Pi payment, no duplicate request can create duplicate payout, and manual/A2U safety controls remain unchanged.
When sample data is not available, rely on unit fixtures and staging tests; do not insert test transactions into Mainnet.
10. Read-only audit facts and limitations
A read-only Mainnet query returned no rows for the selected stakes, withdrawal requests, and Core/Internal investment payment grouping at the time checked. Real-account balance reconciliation therefore cannot be demonstrated from current Mainnet records; use synthetic unit fixtures and an isolated test environment.
Mainnet security advisory output includes broad SECURITY DEFINER function warnings. The wallet endpoint must use only the existing intended service-role path and verified identity; do not broaden browser EXECUTE grants as a workaround.
No GitHub files, Supabase tables/RPCs/data, Render environment variables, deployments, payments, or withdrawals were changed in preparing this document.
